To handle LaTeX escaping in Perl using Raku, you can use several modules depending on whether you need simple character replacement or complex mathematical formatting.

Here are the most common options:

### 1. `LaTeX::Escape`
This is the standard module for basic escaping of special characters (like `&`, `%`, `$`, `#`, `_`, `{`, `}`, `~`, `^`, `\`).

**Example:**
```raku
use LaTeX::Escape;

my $text = "Profit & Loss: 100% & Growth_Rate";
my $escaped = LaTeX::Escape::escape($text);

say $escaped; 
# Output: Profit \& Loss: 100\% \& Growth\_Rate
```

